1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:05,085
A salesperson says every competitor in Miami already uses AI to answer WhatsApp

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,335
messages.

3
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:08,925
Should a small business buy the same tool?

4
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:11,375
A confident pitch can create urgency.

5
00:00:11,390 --> 00:00:13,575
It does not establish proof.

6
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:17,735
SecondLook helps an owner investigate that claim before committing time and money.

7
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,415
Here is the working product.

8
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:21,695
Start with a claim in English or Spanish.

9
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:24,895
Add the company, location, or timeframe when you know them.

10
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:29,285
The first assessment is free, and judges can enter through Try the demo without

11
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:31,155
waiting for an email code.

12
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:34,755
Linkup searches the live web and saves the retrieved sources.

13
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:38,775
Nebius then identifies what the evidence does and does not establish.

14
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:42,995
In this example, finding tools that automate WhatsApp is not evidence that every

15
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:45,415
Miami competitor uses one.

16
00:00:45,430 --> 00:00:48,515
That distinction changes the next question.

17
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:52,715
Instead of repeating a broad search, SecondLook proposes a targeted follow-up around

18
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:54,335
the missing proof.

19
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:58,675
The owner can inspect the first sources before deciding whether to unlock deeper

20
00:00:58,690 --> 00:00:59,350
research.

21
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:04,105
The value is a narrower, more useful investigation, with a record that stays attached

22
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:06,095
to the original claim.

23
00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:08,415
RevenueCat handles the test checkout.

24
00:01:08,430 --> 00:01:10,715
First, a failed purchase:

25
00:01:10,730 --> 00:01:15,255
the free assessment stays intact and paid research remains locked.

26
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:18,575
Then, a valid test purchase unlocks the next step.

27
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:21,895
These are clearly labeled sandbox transactions.

28
00:01:21,910 --> 00:01:23,775
No real money changes hands.

29
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:28,605
The backend verifies the entitlement before running paid research, opening the

30
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:31,335
PDF, or sending an attachment.

31
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:35,595
Access is checked on the server, not inferred from a button in the browser.

32
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:40,435
Missing or expired access blocks paid operations while preserving the first look.

33
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:44,655
With access verified, Linkup performs the focused second search.

34
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:46,855
Nebius builds structured findings:

35
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:50,535
supported, contradicted, or insufficient evidence.

36
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:54,895
Each finding connects to an exact passage from the retrieved material.

37
00:01:54,910 --> 00:01:57,465
Open the source and inspect the words behind the conclusion.

38
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:02,065
A separate review checks whether the passages justify the inference and whether

39
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:05,735
the proposed seller questions are useful.

40
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:08,255
Invalid citations cannot support a finding.

41
00:02:08,270 --> 00:02:12,695
If the search adds no proof, the report keeps the uncertainty visible.

42
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:16,535
In this case, insufficient evidence is the honest result.

43
00:02:16,550 --> 00:02:19,135
That result still helps the owner act.

44
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:23,895
The report explains the gap and prepares concrete questions for the seller.

45
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:29,935
The research record also exposes the model, latency, token usage, and estimated cost.

46
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:34,095
Four English and Spanish regression cases passed with valid citations;

47
00:02:34,110 --> 00:02:37,975
this is a small test set, not a claim of universal accuracy.

48
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:41,735
Finally, preview the generated evidence PDF.

49
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:46,385
Keep the claim, findings, source references, and next questions together in a document

50
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,995
you can download and discuss.

51
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:52,095
Signed-in email users can also request the attachment.

52
00:02:52,110 --> 00:02:58,095
The demo offers the PDF directly, so judges can inspect the deliverable immediately.

53
00:02:58,110 --> 00:03:02,285
SecondLook brings live research, verified paid access, and evidence review into

54
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,105
one decision workflow.

55
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:06,695
A free first look earns the next step.

56
00:03:06,710 --> 00:03:10,135
A reusable brief carries the value beyond the screen.

57
00:03:10,150 --> 00:03:11,775
Try the public app.

58
00:03:11,790 --> 00:03:13,440
Before you buy, check the proof.
